{"nodes":[{"id":"handoff_2026_08_06_step_5_test_redistribution","label":"Handoff: Conformance Step 5 (Test Redistribution)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":"2026-08-06","author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Written so the next session does not re-derive state: it points at CONFORMANCE.md, the git log and CLAUDE.md rather than restating them, and records only environment state, traps and next steps."},{"id":"handoff_2026_08_05_step_4_testbench_migration","label":"Handoff: Conformance Step 4 (Testbench Migration)","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Superseded by the step 5 handoff: its blocker is gone and its next-steps are done."},{"id":"conformance_step_5_test_redistribution","label":"Conformance Step 5 — Test Redistribution","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Tests move out of the host into the package that owns them; a test belongs in a package only if it needs nothing from the host. Moved so far: settings (3 tests), localization-core (locale middleware), localization-core-livewire (language switcher).","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"docs_conformance_plan","label":"docs/CONFORMANCE.md — Conformance Plan","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Its \"Step N is done\" blocks state what was actually found, including where the plan was wrong — the plan is corrected in writing rather than silently."},{"id":"package_testbench","label":"liberusoftware/package-testbench","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Shared boundary suites and test bootstrap so a new boundary rule is one testbench release rather than a 44-repository sweep. Version 1.7.0 at the time of this handoff.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"trap_empty_tests_directory_does_not_publish","label":"Trap: an empty tests/ directory does not publish","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"34 packages shipped 1.2.0 with no tests/ at all; Pest aborts with 'The test directory [tests] does not exist'. The 44-package sweep passed only because the directory was still on disk locally. Fixed with a tracked tests/.gitkeep. Lesson: a fleet sweep does not prove what the tarball contains — only a reinstall does. Second occurrence of this class of error.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"trap_do_not_tag_before_running_shipped_artifact","label":"Trap: do not tag before something has run the shipped artifact","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"testbench 1.3.0 and 1.4.0 were tagged with a boundary suite that could not load. A tag is what Packagist publishes, so it is not recoverable the way a push is.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"trap_define_environment_must_call_parent","label":"Trap: defineEnvironment() overrides must call parent","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"A package overriding defineEnvironment() without parent::defineEnvironment($app) loses the application key PackageTestCase sets (testbench 1.7.0).","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"trap_host_red_between_manifest_bump_and_composer_update","label":"Trap: host goes red between a manifest bump and composer update","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"ModuleValidator compares the manifest against InstalledVersions, so the window between the two is expected red, not a fault.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"trap_wsl_dns_drops_under_parallel_composer","label":"Trap: WSL DNS drops under parallel Composer","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Sweep at -P 2 and retry; higher parallelism loses name resolution.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"task_8_searcher_registry_refactor","label":"Task #8 — searcher registry in search / search-demo split","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Moving SearchService::searchPosts()/searchGroups() and two search-api controller actions into search-demo is a three-package refactor, not a move: searchAll() aggregates over types, so the honest design is a searcher registry in `search` that `search-demo` registers into — which is exactly what CONFORMANCE §3.4 objected to being hardcoded. search's own tests follow the code, not the other way round.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"task_9_adopt_messaging_blog_tests","label":"Task #9 — adopt preserved messaging and blog tests","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Tests preserved at commit 33550079 need adopting into their own repositories.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"blocker_theme_discovery_not_composer_driven","label":"Blocker: theme discovery is not Composer-driven","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"ThemeManager* and ThemeSwitcherTest need installed themes, but discovery reads base_path('themes') rather than InstalledVersions the way ModuleDiscovery does, and Testbench's base path is its own skeleton. Fixing it also closes the theme-support §4 row, where three successive guards had to be loosened to make the package bootable.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"risk_package_ci_never_observed_green","label":"Risk: package CI has not been observed green","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Runs on liberusoftware/module-* queued over an hour; every suite passes locally with the same command CI runs, but nobody has seen the workflows themselves pass since the migration. Check before assuming.","entity_type":"concept"},{"id":"working_agreement_verify_before_asserting","label":"Working agreement: verify before asserting","file_type":"document","source_file":"docs/handoffs/2026-08-06-step-5-test-redistribution.md","source_location":null,"source_url":null,"captured_at":null,"author":null,"contributor":null,"rationale":"Mutation-test a new rule; outward-facing steps get confirmed; the plan is corrected in writing when wrong; no Claude attribution footers.","entity_type":"concept"}],"edges":[{"source":"handoff_2026_08_06_step_5_test_redistribution","target":"handoff_2026_08_05_step_4_testbench_migration","relation":"cites","confidence":"EXTRACTED","confidence_score":1,"source_file":"